<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">Educational Summary</div>
  <div class="card-body">
  <p><strong>Introduction to PEERAMID 2:</strong> This summary provides an overview of the PEERAMID 2, a <em>clinical instrument</em> designed to assess neurodevelopmental functions in children aged 9 to 14.</p>
  <p><strong>Purpose of this cognitive battery:</strong> It assists professionals in identifying strengths and weaknesses in various developmental areas, aiding in diagnosis and intervention planning.</p>
  <p><strong>Target Audience:</strong> The PEERAMID 2 is intended for use by trained professionals, including pediatricians, psychologists, and educational specialists.</p>
  <hr>
  <h3>Evolution and Development</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Origins of the Assessment:</strong> Developed from earlier instruments like PEER and PEEX.</li>
    <li><strong>Refinement Process:</strong> Planned through a Robert Wood Johnson Foundation grant.</li>
    <li><strong>Key Revisions:</strong> Added phonological awareness, more memory emphasis, improved visual processing tasks.</li>
  </ul>
  <hr>
  <h3>General Information and Administration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Administration Time:</strong> Approximately one hour.</li>
    <li><strong>Normative Data:</strong> Provided for ages 9-14, with consideration of local norms.</li>
    <li><strong>Required Materials:</strong> Response Book, Stimulus Book, squash ball, cup, pencil, stopwatch.</li>
    <li><strong>Components:</strong> Fine motor/graphomotor, language, gross motor, memory, visual processing sections.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">Main Sections</div>
  <div class="card-body">
<ul>
  <li><strong>Fine Motor/Graphomotor Functions</strong>: Assesses motor skills related to writing.</li>
  <li><strong>Language Functions</strong>: Evaluates various language parameters, including phonological awareness and comprehension.</li>
  <li><strong>Gross Motor Functions</strong>: Provides information about motor skills and neuromaturational signs.</li>
  <li><strong>Memory Functions</strong>: Assesses different types of memory (short-term, sequential).</li>
  <li><strong>Visual Processing Functions</strong>: Examines ability to process and interpret visual information.</li>
</ul>
 </div>
</div>


<!-- Left–Right Discrimination -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Left–Right Discrimination</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_lr')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_lr" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> The examiner should provide clear, slow instructions:<br>
      “I am going to give you some instructions. I want you to listen carefully and follow them as best as you can. Please do not repeat the instructions aloud.”</p>

      <p><strong>Instruction Sequence:</strong><br>
      The examiner gives five instructions, one at a time. The last three instructions should be read slowly and, importantly, the examiner should turn to face the child during the final three instructions to ensure clarity and avoid confusion.</p>

      <p><strong>Example commands include:</strong><br>
      “Raise your left hand.”<br>
      “Touch your right ear.”<br>
      “Put your left hand on your right knee.”<br>
      “Point to your right foot.”<br>
      “Stand with your right foot forward.”</p>
    </div>

    <label for="lr_score">Correct Responses (0–5):</label>
    <input id="lr_score" type="number" class="form-control mb-2" min="0" max="5" placeholder="Score (0–5)">

    <label for="lr_notes">Notes:</label>
    <textarea id="lr_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., Midline confusion, sequencing errors..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreLeftRightDiscrimination()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="lr_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreLeftRightDiscrimination() {
  const score = document.getElementById('lr_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('lr_notes').value;
  const output =
    "Task: Left–Right Discrimination" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;
  document.getElementById('lr_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Lateral Preference (Hand/Eye Dominance) -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-info">
  <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">Lateral Preference (Hand/Eye Dominance)</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_lat_pref')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_lat_pref" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> Ask the child to mimic functional tasks such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>“Show me how you throw a ball.”</li>
        <li>“Pretend you are hammering a nail into the desk.”</li>
        <li>“Pretend you are brushing your teeth.”</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Next, roll a response book into a tube and hand it to the child at midline. Say:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>“Look at me through this telescope I just made.”</li>
        <li>Then: “Look up at the ceiling.”</li>
        <li>“Now, look at the door.”</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="lat_pref_score">Score:</label>
    <select id="lat_pref_score" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Mixed</option>
      <option value="1">1 = Left hand/eye</option>
      <option value="2">2 = Right hand/eye</option>
    </select>

    <label for="lat_pref_notes">Notes:</label>
    <textarea id="lat_pref_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., mixed dominance, favoring left eye..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreLateralPreference()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="lat_pref_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreLateralPreference() {
  const score = document.getElementById('lat_pref_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('lat_pref_notes').value;
  const output =
    "Task: Lateral Preference (Hand/Eye Dominance)" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;
  document.getElementById('lat_pref_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Motor Sequential Imitation -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Motor Sequential Imitation</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_motor_seq')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_motor_seq" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Rationale:</strong> This task assesses motor procedural memory — the brain’s ability to encode, store, and retrieve specific fine motor patterns.</p>
      <p><em>It is crucial for:</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Writing fluency</li>
        <li>Typing</li>
        <li>Instrument performance</li>
        <li>Other sequential hand-based tasks</li>
      </ul>
      <p>It also overlaps with attention, directionality, and fine motor planning, making it a key crossover measure in both memory and graphomotor function domains.</p>
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> “Now we’re going to see how well you can get your fingers to remember patterns. Put both hands up in front of you like me. I’m going to move my fingers in a certain order. I’ll do it three times, then I’d like you to do exactly the same thing — three times. Use your [dominant hand]. Don’t start until I’ve shown you all three demonstrations.”</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Demonstrate each sequence three times, using your opposite hand (mirror image).</li>
        <li>Child imitates using their dominant hand immediately afterward.</li>
        <li>Allow self-correction during imitation. If self-correction occurs, require three perfect sequences consecutively.</li>
        <li>Do not re-demonstrate for credit scoring purposes.</li>
        <li>You may repeat a sequence for exploration/teaching, but do not award credit.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="motor_seq_score"><strong>Performance:</strong></label>
    <select id="motor_seq_score" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct 3 consecutive reproductions</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect or needed re-demonstration</option>
    </select>

    <label for="motor_seq_notes"><strong>Behavioral Notes:</strong></label>
    <textarea id="motor_seq_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., false starts, direction confusion..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreMotorSequentialImitation()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="motor_seq_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>

    <div class="mt-4">
      <strong>Interpretation:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Difficulty with recall:</strong> May suggest procedural memory deficits.</li>
        <li><strong>False starts or finger confusion:</strong> Could indicate fine motor or motor planning problems.</li>
        <li><strong>Delay or frustration:</strong> May reflect working memory or attention difficulties.</li>
        <li><strong>Directionality confusion:</strong> Often seen in younger children or those with visuospatial challenges.</li>
      </ul>
      <strong>Compare with:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Verbal Instructions (Part B) — for working memory comparison.</li>
        <li>Graphomotor tasks — to determine memory vs. execution issues.</li>
        <li>Writing samples — to examine functional manifestation of motor sequences.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreMotorSequentialImitation() {
  const score = document.getElementById('motor_seq_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('motor_seq_notes').value;
  const output =
    "Task: Motor Sequential Imitation" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;
  document.getElementById('motor_seq_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Imitative Finger Movement -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Imitative Finger Movement</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_ifm')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_ifm" class="collapsible-section mb-3" style="display: none;">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> “Put your hands up like this. I want you to do the same things with your hands that I do with mine, as if I were your mirror. You should look at my fingers, but don’t look at your own fingers.”</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Oppose thumb and index finger (1-2) near the ear, hold 1 second.</li>
        <li>Oppose fingers 1-4, hold 1 second.</li>
        <li>Oppose 1-5, then 1-3, each held for 1 second.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="ifm_score">Score:</label>
    <select id="ifm_score" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Present (can imitate)</option>
      <option value="1">1 = Absent (cannot imitate)</option>
    </select>

    <label for="ifm_notes">Notes:</label>
    <textarea id="ifm_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="Describe mirror accuracy, presence of synkinesia, etc."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreImitativeFingerMovement()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="ifm_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreImitativeFingerMovement() {
  const score = document.getElementById('ifm_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('ifm_notes').value;
  const output =
    "Task: Imitative Finger Movement" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;
  document.getElementById('ifm_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Rapid Alternating Movement -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Rapid Alternating Movement</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_ram')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_ram" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> “Hold your arm above your head, squeeze the ball as hard as you can, and pretend you are turning a light bulb back and forth. Do this as fast as you can.”</p>

      <p><strong>Rationale:</strong> This task assesses rapid alternating movements (RAM), which are part of cerebellar function and can provide insight into:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Motor coordination</li>
        <li>Motor sequencing ability</li>
        <li>Inhibitory control</li>
        <li>Upper limb dexterity</li>
      </ul>

      <p>RAM difficulties may appear in various developmental, neurological, or motor planning disorders. The test mimics real-world activities like turning doorknobs or twisting jar lids.</p>

      <p><strong>Tips:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Model the motion for the child before requesting their imitation.</li>
        <li>Note hand dominance and speed consistency.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="ram_score"><strong>Performance:</strong></label>
    <select id="ram_score" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Smooth, rapid, symmetrical motion</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Irregular, slow, or asymmetrical motion</option>
    </select>

    <label for="ram_notes"><strong>Behavioral Notes:</strong></label>
    <textarea id="ram_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., tremors, rhythm issues, switching delay..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreRapidAlternatingMovement()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="ram_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreRapidAlternatingMovement() {
  const score = document.getElementById('ram_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('ram_notes').value;
  const output =
    "Task: Rapid Alternating Movement" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;
  document.getElementById('ram_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Sequential Finger Opposition -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Sequential Finger Opposition</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_sfo')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_sfo" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> "Now I am going to move my fingers in a special way. I want you to watch very closely and when I am finished, I would like you to move your fingers in the same order, the same way I did. You can look at your fingers as you do this. I want you to use the tips of your fingers and make a perfect O, the way I am doing."</p>

      <p>The examiner will oppose their second, third, fourth, and then fifth fingers against their thumb in sequential order three times. The examiner will then ask the patient to repeat 6 cycles under time conditions.</p>
    </div>

    <label for="sfo_demo"><strong>Needed more than one demonstration?</strong></label>
    <select id="sfo_demo" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Yes</option>
      <option value="1">1 = No</option>
    </select>

    <label for="sfo_synkinesia"><strong>Synkinesia or associated movement?</strong></label>
    <select id="sfo_synkinesia" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Present</option>
      <option value="1">1 = Absent</option>
    </select>

    <label for="sfo_distal"><strong>Distal function (fingertips form a perfect 'O'):</strong></label>
    <select id="sfo_distal" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Poor (fewer than 5 cycles)</option>
      <option value="1">1 = Good (5–6 cycles)</option>
    </select>

    <label for="sfo_speed"><strong>Speed (in seconds):</strong></label>
    <input id="sfo_speed" type="number" class="form-control mb-2" placeholder="e.g. 12.5">

    <label for="sfo_seq_errors"><strong>Sequence errors:</strong></label>
    <select id="sfo_seq_errors" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect on >1 cycle</option>
      <option value="1">1 = Correct on 5–6 cycles</option>
    </select>

    <label for="sfo_notes"><strong>Behavioral Notes:</strong></label>
    <textarea id="sfo_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="Describe any delays, awkwardness, corrections..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreSequentialFingerOpposition()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="sfo_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreSequentialFingerOpposition() {
  const demo = document.getElementById('sfo_demo').value;
  const synkinesia = document.getElementById('sfo_synkinesia').value;
  const distal = document.getElementById('sfo_distal').value;
  const speed = document.getElementById('sfo_speed').value;
  const seqErrors = document.getElementById('sfo_seq_errors').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('sfo_notes').value;

  const output =
    "Task: Sequential Finger Opposition" + "<br>" +
    "Needed More Than One Demonstration: " + (demo == "0" ? "Yes" : "No") + "<br>" +
    "Synkinesia or Associated Movement: " + (synkinesia == "0" ? "Present" : "Absent") + "<br>" +
    "Distal Function (Perfect O's): " + (distal == "0" ? "Poor (<5 cycles)" : "Good (5–6 cycles)") + "<br>" +
    "Speed: " + speed + " seconds" + "<br>" +
    "Sequence Errors: " + (seqErrors == "0" ? "Incorrect on >1 cycle" : "Correct on 5–6 cycles") + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;

  document.getElementById('sfo_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Alternating Fists -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-primary">
  <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Alternating Fists</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_af')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_af" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> “Do exactly what I do. Don't start until I'm finished.”</p>

      <p>The examiner extends both arms directly in front of the body, parallel to the ground. The examiner then alternates hand movements by opening one fist while closing the other, repeating this motion three times in sequence.</p>

      <p><strong>Tips:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Watch for midline confusion, motor overflow, or loss of rhythm.</li>
        <li>Encourage the child to stay in rhythm and maintain proper hand positioning throughout.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="af_score"><strong>Performance:</strong></label>
    <select id="af_score" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Smooth, rhythmic, and mirrored correctly</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Irregular, loss of rhythm, or mirrored incorrectly</option>
    </select>

    <label for="af_notes"><strong>Behavioral Notes:</strong></label>
    <textarea id="af_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., hand confusion, starting early, rhythm break..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="scoreAlternatingFists()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="af_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreAlternatingFists() {
  const score = document.getElementById('af_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('af_notes').value;
  
  let scoreMeaning = "";
  if (score === "1") {
    scoreMeaning = "Smooth, rhythmic, and mirrored correctly";
  } else if (score === "0") {
    scoreMeaning = "Irregular, loss of rhythm, or mirrored incorrectly";
  }

  const output =
    "Task: Alternating Fists" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + " = " + scoreMeaning + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;

  document.getElementById('af_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Catch Ball in Cup -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-info">
  <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">Catch Ball in Cup</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_cup')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_cup" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Instruction:</strong> “I want you to throw the ball above your head to catch it in the cup. Use either hand to throw the ball, whichever you want. You don't have to throw it very high, but make sure it goes above your head. You can practice 3 times. Good? Okay. Now toss it up 10 times and try to catch it. Let's see how many times you can get the ball in the cup.”</p>

      <p>The examiner provides a small foam ball and a lightweight plastic cup. The child may use either hand for throwing. After three practice tosses, the child attempts 10 consecutive tosses and catches.</p>
    </div>

    <label for="cup_score"><strong>Successful Catches (out of 10 attempts):</strong></label>
    <input id="cup_score" type="number" class="form-control mb-2" min="0" max="10" placeholder="0–10">

    <label for="cup_notes"><strong>Behavioral Notes:</strong></label>
    <textarea id="cup_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., ball height, timing, use of both hands..."></textarea>

    <button class="btn btn-info" onclick="scoreCatchBallInCup()">Generate Output</button>
    <div id="cup_output" class="section-output mt-2"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
function scoreCatchBallInCup() {
  const score = document.getElementById('cup_score').value;
  const notes = document.getElementById('cup_notes').value;

  let scoreMeaning = "";
  if (score >= 8) {
    scoreMeaning = "Excellent hand-eye coordination";
  } else if (score >= 5) {
    scoreMeaning = "Adequate coordination with occasional misses";
  } else {
    scoreMeaning = "Difficulty with timing and coordination";
  }

  const output =
    "Task: Catch Ball in Cup" + "<br>" +
    "Score: " + score + "/10 = " + scoreMeaning + "<br>" +
    "Interpretation: " + notes;

  document.getElementById('cup_output').innerHTML = output;
}
</script>
<!-- Hopping in Place -->
<div class="card mb-4 border-info">
  <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">Hopping in Place</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_hip')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_hip" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
