<div class="card mb-4 border-dark">
  <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">Rapid Verbal Recall (RVR)</div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <button class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm mb-2" onclick="toggleSection('inst_rvr')">Show Instructions</button>
    <div id="inst_rvr" class="collapsible-section mb-3">
      <p><strong>Rationale:</strong> This task evaluates a child's understanding of temporal sequences and the ability to access long-term memory (e.g., days, months), use active working memory to reorder known sequences, demonstrate automatized recall, and comprehend and manipulate temporally complex language. Difficulty here may reflect sequential memory weakness, inattention, or poor retrieval fluency, all of which impact real-world planning and academic tasks.</p>

      <p><strong>Instructions:</strong> This task is administered after the gross motor assessment. Examiner says: “Now I'm going to ask you a few questions.” Only items 3 and 4 may be repeated once in their entirety. Responses with a latency greater than 5 seconds should be flagged as hesitation.</p>

      <p><strong>Prompts:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Question 1:</strong> “Tell me the days of the week backwards starting with Thursday.”<br>
        <em>Expected response:</em> Thursday, Wednesday, Tuesday, Monday, Sunday, Saturday, Friday.</li>
        <li><strong>Question 2:</strong> “What month comes directly before March?”<br>
        <em>Expected response:</em> February.</li>
        <li><strong>Question 3:</strong> “During a race, a runner finishes at 11:30. Another finished 15 minutes earlier. What time did the fastest runner finish?”<br>
        <em>Expected response:</em> 11:15.</li>
        <li><strong>Question 4:</strong> “John does his science homework before he does his English but after his math. What does John do second?”<br>
        <em>Expected response:</em> Science.</li>
        <li><strong>Question 5:</strong> “What month comes right before September?”<br>
        <em>Expected response:</em> August.</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>Clinical Interpretation:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Errors on Question 1 (days backwards):</strong> Suggests sequential memory weakness, poor automatized recall, or difficulty reversing ordered sequences.</li>
        <li><strong>Errors on Question 2 (month before March) or Question 5 (month before September):</strong> Suggest difficulty accessing temporal sequences from long-term memory or weaker semantic time mapping.</li>
        <li><strong>Errors on Question 3 (race time calculation):</strong> Suggest impaired working memory, slowed mental math manipulation, or difficulty integrating temporal concepts with numeric reasoning.</li>
        <li><strong>Errors on Question 4 (homework sequence):</strong> Suggest difficulty with multi-step verbal reasoning, executive dysfunction (planning and ordering information).</li>
        <li><strong>Frequent hesitations (>5 seconds):</strong> Reflect slowed retrieval speed, weak processing fluency, or attentional inefficiency.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <label for="rvr_score"><strong>Correct Responses (0–5):</strong></label>
