      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_a2">Item 2: Draw small and middle sized circles inside the two big circles. (Cognitive Demand: Embedded spatial prepositions)</label>
    <select id="vi_a2" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_a3">Item 3: Put a circle around the small X that's farthest away from the small square. (Cognitive Demand: Distance-based reasoning)</label>
    <select id="vi_a3" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_a4">Item 4: Make a dot inside the four dots and then make a circle that only goes around it. (Cognitive Demand: Object isolation plus containment)</label>
    <select id="vi_a4" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_a5">Item 5: Make a circle in the big square and then make a square in the middle one. (Cognitive Demand: Sequential shape-in-shape)</label>
    <select id="vi_a5" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <h5>Part B: Active Working Memory</h5>

    <label for="vi_b6">Item 6: Before you make four X's above the middle square, draw a line connecting the two circles. (Cognitive Demand: Temporal reversal and working memory)</label>
    <select id="vi_b6" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_b7">Item 7: Draw five squares at the top of the page if there are more than 14 dots. (Cognitive Demand: Conditional reasoning and visual scan)</label>
    <select id="vi_b7" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_b8">Item 8: Put three dots above the thick line after you've made a square and a circle underneath it. (Cognitive Demand: Temporal sequencing and shape placement)</label>
    <select id="vi_b8" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_b9">Item 9: Make small circles under the small X's and small X's under the big circles. (Cognitive Demand: Alternating sequencing by shape and size)</label>
    <select id="vi_b9" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_b10">Item 10: Draw four circles next to the shortest line, but first draw one X and two dots underneath it. (Cognitive Demand: Dual order execution with spatial logic)</label>
    <select id="vi_b10" class="form-select mb-2">
      <option value="1">1 = Correct</option>
      <option value="0">0 = Incorrect</option>
    </select>

    <label for="vi_notes">General Behavioral Notes:</label>
    <textarea id="vi_notes" class="form-control mb-2" rows="2" placeholder="E.g., impulsivity, inattention, difficulty sequencing, confusion between objects..."></textarea>

